  "_status": "SEED (~90 entries). Target for v1 is 600-900 entries, which is enough to cover the overwhelming majority of real Indian consumer spend - a small number of merchants account for most transactions, and user rules cover the tail. Research pass is expanding this.",
  "_design": {
    "matching": "The merchant string from SMS is normalized (uppercase, strip UPI/ P2M/ P2A/ prefixes, strip trailing ref digits, collapse whitespace and punctuation) then matched: exact alias -> token containment -> VPA handle. First hit wins.",
    "aliases": "Real SMS rarely says 'Swiggy'. It says SWIGGY, SWIGGYUPI, BUNDLTECH, or swiggy@axisbank. Every known surface form goes in aliases.",
    "vpa_handles": "Suffixes like @okaxis or @ybl identify the PSP, not the merchant, and must never be used to categorize. Only full VPA prefixes (e.g. swiggy@) are meaningful.",
    "confidence": "A dictionary hit is high confidence (0.95). Token-containment is medium (0.75) and still auto-applies but is flagged as correctable in the UI."
  },
